206. Reverse Linked List

Explanation:

🧠 Goal
Reverse the direction of every pointer in the list.

Original:
1 → 2 → 3 → 4 → null

Reversed:
4 → 3 → 2 → 1 → null

👉 We are NOT reversing values.
👉 We are reversing links (arrows).

⭐ Core Idea

Use 3 pointers:

prev → previous node
curr → current node
next → next node (saved)

🔥 Golden Rule (MOST IMPORTANT)

👉 SAVE BEFORE YOU BREAK

When you reverse a pointer, you lose the forward connection.

So always store:
next = curr.next;

first.

✅ Algorithm Steps

Repeat while curr != null:

1️⃣ Save next node
next = curr.next;

2️⃣ Reverse pointer
curr.next = prev;

3️⃣ Move prev forward
prev = curr;

4️⃣ Move curr forward
curr = next;

⭐ After Loop Ends

curr becomes null.

prev will be pointing to the new head.

👉 Always return:

return prev;
NOT the old head.


Code:

/**
 * Definition for singly-linked list.
 * public class ListNode {
 *     int val;
 *     ListNode next;
 *     ListNode() {}
 *     ListNode(int val) { this.val = val; }
 *     ListNode(int val, ListNode next) { this.val = val; this.next = next; }
 * }
 */
 
class Solution {
    public ListNode reverseList(ListNode head) {
        ListNode prev = null;
        ListNode curr = head;

        while(curr!=null){
            ListNode next = curr.next;
            curr.next = prev;
            prev= curr;
            curr= next;
        }
        return prev;
    }
}
